WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.539 --> 00:00:05.330
Marvel's Black Panther has made its theatrical
debut, and moviegoers couldn't be more excited.

00:00:05.330 --> 00:00:10.040
As one of the MCU's few superheroes not played
by a dude named Chris, the Black Panther is

00:00:10.040 --> 00:00:14.559
a powerful new addition to Marvel's roster
of on-screen heroes, and he brings an entire

00:00:14.559 --> 00:00:17.700
country of awesome sci-fi tech and culture
with him.

00:00:17.700 --> 00:00:21.730
But now that the credits have rolled and your
vibranium suit is all out of energy, there's

00:00:21.730 --> 00:00:24.720
still something we gotta talk about: that
ending.

00:00:24.720 --> 00:00:28.369
While the plot wrapped up without much in
the way of loose ends, there are still plenty

00:00:28.369 --> 00:00:31.110
of questions we can ask about what it all
means.

00:00:31.110 --> 00:00:31.920
And of course...

00:00:36.100 --> 00:00:37.600
...spoilers ahead.

00:00:37.610 --> 00:00:39.510
What's next for Wakanda?

00:00:39.510 --> 00:00:43.150
Killmonger's insurrection caused some sharp
divisions among the four united tribes of

00:00:43.150 --> 00:00:48.070
Wakanda — the Border Tribe played a particularly
nasty role in supporting Killmonger's plan

00:00:48.070 --> 00:00:50.870
to send vibranium weapons all over the world.

00:00:50.870 --> 00:00:55.940
The end of the film saw W'Kabi surrender to
Okoye after a battle between the Border Tribe,

00:00:55.940 --> 00:00:58.220
the Mountain Tribe, and Okoye's warriors.

00:00:58.220 --> 00:01:00.690
Peace is restored to Wakanda, right?

00:01:00.690 --> 00:01:01.690
Or is it?

00:01:01.690 --> 00:01:05.680
We know that the King of Wakanda is the absolute
monarch of the country, since Killmonger was

00:01:05.680 --> 00:01:10.330
able to completely reverse the nation's isolationist
policies with the snap of a finger.

00:01:10.330 --> 00:01:14.330
But even with an absolute monarchy, the people
being governed still need to be cool with

00:01:14.330 --> 00:01:15.790
the person in charge.

00:01:15.790 --> 00:01:19.780
Now that the Border Tribe openly rebelled
against T'Challa, what's their status with

00:01:19.780 --> 00:01:21.490
the country itself?

00:01:21.490 --> 00:01:25.770
And since M'Baku and the Mountain Tribe came
to T'Challa's rescue, does that meant that

00:01:25.770 --> 00:01:28.620
they'll be involved in running the country
going forward?

00:01:28.620 --> 00:01:32.450
While we don't know any of the answers to
these questions now, it seems that the political

00:01:32.450 --> 00:01:35.950
intrigue going on within Wakanda's borders
has only just started.

00:01:35.950 --> 00:01:37.560
Wakanda and the world

00:01:37.560 --> 00:01:42.430
At the end of the movie, T'Challa decides
to open his nation up to the world after centuries

00:01:42.430 --> 00:01:43.430
of isolation.

00:01:43.430 --> 00:01:47.950
It's a logical decision considering the consequences
of his father's decision to leave young Erik

00:01:47.950 --> 00:01:51.729
Stevens, who grows up to become the usurper
Killmonger, in Oakland.

00:01:51.729 --> 00:01:56.060
By sharing its technology and science with
the rest of the globe, Wakanda will undoubtedly

00:01:56.060 --> 00:01:58.830
have a major effect on, well, everything.

00:01:58.830 --> 00:02:01.970
Will we see those effects take place in some
way in future MCU movies?

00:02:01.970 --> 00:02:06.020
Or would that move the cinematic universe
a little too far from our own to still be

00:02:06.020 --> 00:02:07.020
relatable?

00:02:07.020 --> 00:02:11.209
It'll be interesting to see how — or if
— other MCU movies decide to tackle this

00:02:11.209 --> 00:02:12.709
new continuity wrinkle.

00:02:12.709 --> 00:02:16.819
Though, there is one probable application
of this new super-science…

00:02:16.819 --> 00:02:17.969
Marvelous medicine

00:02:17.969 --> 00:02:22.290
When Agent Everett Ross took a bullet for
Nakia, he severely injured his spine.

00:02:22.290 --> 00:02:26.310
But after spending one night in Wakanda and
receiving medical treatment, he was fully

00:02:26.310 --> 00:02:27.310
healed.

00:02:27.310 --> 00:02:31.219
That probably means James Rhodes, better known
as War Machine, may be paying a visit to Shuri's

00:02:31.219 --> 00:02:35.370
lab to get his own spine fixed up after he
was shot with a laser beam and slammed into

00:02:35.370 --> 00:02:37.469
the ground in Captain America: Civil War.

00:02:37.469 --> 00:02:40.639
We already know Shuri's hard at work at rehabilitating
Bucky.

00:02:40.639 --> 00:02:42.340
Why wouldn't Rhodie get the same treatment?

00:02:42.340 --> 00:02:46.409
We've seen the War Machine armor in action
in Wakanda during the trailer for Infinity

00:02:46.409 --> 00:02:50.309
War, so it's a good bet that Rhodes will be
up and at'em by the time that movie drops,

00:02:50.309 --> 00:02:52.870
all thanks to that wacky Wakandan health care
system.

00:02:52.870 --> 00:02:55.639
A vibranium arsenal in the offing

00:02:55.639 --> 00:02:59.579
We've known about that miraculous metal vibranium
since Steve Rogers first got his shield in

00:02:59.579 --> 00:03:01.540
Captain America: The First Avenger.

00:03:01.540 --> 00:03:04.969
But outside of having a cool name and being
pretty tough, we haven't known much about

00:03:04.969 --> 00:03:07.870
what the stuff can actually do — until now.

00:03:07.870 --> 00:03:11.349
Killmonger's plan to send powerful weapons
to agents all over the world may have been

00:03:11.349 --> 00:03:15.799
a pretty mean plan for world domination, but
it also gave us our first glimpse into how

00:03:15.799 --> 00:03:17.730
powerful Wakanda's weapons can be.

00:03:17.730 --> 00:03:21.840
That means that when Thanos and his horde
of alien super-jerks show up on Earth in Infinity

00:03:21.840 --> 00:03:26.349
War, humanity will have a fighting chance
thanks to King T'Challa and his army.

00:03:26.349 --> 00:03:27.370
Coming to America

00:03:27.370 --> 00:03:31.569
In addition to starting the super-tech exchange
in America, we see T'Challa spending some

00:03:31.569 --> 00:03:34.250
time outside of Wakanda at the movie's end.

00:03:34.250 --> 00:03:38.129
Surely with his newfound appreciation for
helping others outside of Wakanda's borders

00:03:38.129 --> 00:03:42.419
we can expect to see the Black Panther spend
some time fighting bad guys in the United

00:03:42.419 --> 00:03:43.419
States, right?

00:03:43.419 --> 00:03:47.700
It's entirely possible that Black Panther
2 might show T'Challa's quest to understand

00:03:47.700 --> 00:03:51.629
the rest of the world now that he's looking
to make Wakanda a member of the international

00:03:51.629 --> 00:03:52.629
community.

00:03:52.629 --> 00:03:56.639
And if Wakanda is looking to influence other
countries, it goes without saying that some

00:03:56.639 --> 00:03:58.790
of that influence will come back the other
way.

00:03:58.790 --> 00:04:03.180
Sure, Wakanda has amazing super-suits and
techno-cars...but just wait 'til they try

00:04:03.180 --> 00:04:04.389
Dippin' Dots!

00:04:04.389 --> 00:04:06.359
Wakanda will never be the same.

00:04:06.359 --> 00:04:08.209
The future of the MCU

00:04:08.209 --> 00:04:12.409
Above all else, the end of Black Panther shows
that Marvel can find a way to stick superheroes

00:04:12.409 --> 00:04:14.540
into just about any story you can imagine.

00:04:14.540 --> 00:04:19.090
We've already seen a super-powered heist in
Ant-Man, and a superhero spy story in Captain

00:04:19.090 --> 00:04:24.290
America: The Winter Soldier, while Thor Ragnarok
was basically a...well...look, it's not really

00:04:24.290 --> 00:04:27.240
clear what the hell Thor Ragnarok was, but
it was really awesome.

00:04:28.600 --> 00:04:30.280
"YES!"

00:04:32.380 --> 00:04:37.840
Black Panther is many things — an Afrofuturist
sci-fi epic, a Shakespearean family drama,

00:04:37.840 --> 00:04:42.370
a poignant commentary on racial divisions
and colonization — but it's also an engaging

00:04:42.370 --> 00:04:47.210
and engrossing adventure that takes conventional
movie wisdom and chucks it out the window.

00:04:47.210 --> 00:04:51.730
Marvel's decision to finally buck the trend
of making movies starring "dudes named Chris"

00:04:51.730 --> 00:04:53.570
means this is just the beginning.

00:04:53.570 --> 00:04:57.160
Don't be surprised to see even more characters
pulled from Marvel Comics' deep roster of

00:04:57.160 --> 00:05:00.820
heroes hailing from all different backgrounds
and origins before too long.

00:05:00.820 --> 00:05:05.120
And that raises one important question: just
how long do we have to wait to see Kamala

00:05:05.120 --> 00:05:06.800
Khan get her own movie?

00:05:06.800 --> 00:05:07.800
Thanks for watching!

00:05:07.800 --> 00:05:10.730
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:05:10.730 --> 00:05:13.060
Plus check out all this other cool stuff we
know you'll love too.

